const body = `<h1>1.6a — Split Between Friends</h1>

<p>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Expand Application. You've seen the basic pattern.
    Now stretch it — add features, solve new problems. Same skeleton handles
    every new requirement.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>The basic tip calculator handles one person. Extend it to split the bill.</p>

    <p><strong>Add these variables to your existing TipCalculator:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>int numberOfPeople</code> — how many are splitting the bill</li>
        <li><code>double perPerson</code> — what each person owes</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Modify your program:</strong></p>
    <ol>
        <li>After calculating the total, divide by <code>numberOfPeople</code> to
            get <code>perPerson</code></li>
        <li>Print: "Each of N people pays: $X.XX"</li>
        <li>Print: "Tip per person: $X.XX" (tip divided by number of people)</li>
    </ol>

    <p><strong>Test:</strong> $87.50 bill, 18% tip, 3 people. Each should pay
    $34.42 (total is $103.25, divided by 3).</p>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <p>
            Which section of the three-step pattern changed when you added this
            feature? Did you need to change Step 1? Step 2? Step 3? Or all three?
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Add Sales Tax</h3>
        <p>
            Add a tax rate variable (like 8.25%). Apply tax to the bill
            <em>before</em> calculating the tip. Where does this new calculation
            go in the three-step pattern — before the tip calculation or after?
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

